  "description": "Discontinued. This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic Hemlock.\n\nThe Hemlock was Cotic's first full suspension bike: a super versatile trail riding animal. Proof that one bike really can do it all, it had the full-on, grab-it-by-the-scruff-of-the-neck handling Cotic is known for, with two distinct travel flavours.\n\nThe 120mm 'short' travel rocker gave punchy performance and a sharper platform, a great all round UK ride from trail centre to tech. The 150mm 'long' rocker gave plush, bottomless performance for big mountain holidays and epic rock fields. With a quick swap of rocker link and tyres, the bike went from speedy trail demon to mighty mountain flattener and back again. Keep two suspension bikes in the garage? Not any more.",
